00:09:56.365 --> 00:09:59.090
And I guess I'll start by

00:09:59.090 --> 00:10:01.535
taking on a challenge that someone asked me recently

00:10:01.535 --> 00:10:04.885
which is to define a blockchain in 10 words or less.

00:10:04.885 --> 00:10:06.095
So, what is a blockchain?

00:10:06.095 --> 00:10:07.960
Well, let me try to define it in

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:10.665
10 words or less and then we'll kind of dig into the words.

00:10:10.665 --> 00:10:12.370
So, a blockchain really is

00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:15.790
a data structure that has a number of critical properties, right?

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:18.630
So the properties are basically liveness,

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:20.950
which means that anyone can write to

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:24.215
the blockchain and there's no way to prevent you from writing to the blockchain.

00:10:24.215 --> 00:10:25.620
Right, we call that liveness.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:29.150
When you write to the Blockchain obviously sometimes there's

00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:33.410
a transaction fee associated with that but if you're willing to pay the transaction fee,

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:35.805
you cannot be prevented from writing to the blockchain.

00:10:35.805 --> 00:10:37.140
So that's liveness.

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:39.960
Persistence means that once the data is written to the blockchain,

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:41.380
it can never be removed.

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:45.935
And typically, the way we achieve persistence is by replicating the blockchain.

00:10:45.935 --> 00:10:49.620
This data structure replicating in many times all over the world.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:52.300
So that if you're gonna remove something from the blockchain you have to

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:55.585
remove it from all the replicas or a majority of the replicas.

00:10:55.585 --> 00:10:58.610
So that's persistence and you notice there's a little star

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:02.270
there because typically persistence is achieved under

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:06.620
certain assumptions basically say the adversary has less than 51% of

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:09.080
the computing power in the network or

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:11.935
there are other ideas that are coming up about

00:11:11.935 --> 00:11:14.215
less than a certain amount of the stake

00:11:14.215 --> 00:11:16.720
of the funds in the network less than a certain amount of

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:19.620
the space that the network uses and so on and so forth.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:23.150
But persistence typically is achieved under certain assumptions.

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:26.600
And once you have liveness and persistence,

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:29.880
the other important property that's implied by that is what's called consensus,

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:32.300
which essentially means that anyone that's using

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:35.720
the blockchain agrees on the current state of the blockchain.

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:38.650
That is, we all agree on what data currently,

00:11:38.650 --> 00:11:41.370
resides on the blockchain. Okay, good.

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:44.195
So, those are kind of the three properties that

00:11:44.195 --> 00:11:46.615
blockchains provide to us.

00:11:46.615 --> 00:11:50.280
But fundamentally, I want you to remember it is just a data structure for

00:11:50.280 --> 00:11:53.710
managing data and it just happens to provide these properties.

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:57.365
Now, these properties enable a tremendous number of applications.

00:11:57.365 --> 00:11:58.830
The most--

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:01.440
the simplest one is something is in the cryptocurrency, right?

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:03.240
If you have liveness and persistence,

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:05.580
essentially this means that

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:06.920
if somebody sends you money,

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:08.165
there is no, you know,

00:12:08.165 --> 00:12:11.410
a crypto token say there is no way to take to undo

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:12.530
that transaction because of

00:12:12.530 --> 00:12:15.140
the persistence properties or rather I should be more precise,

00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:17.045
there's no way to remove the transaction

00:12:17.045 --> 00:12:19.335
from the blockchain because of the persistence property.

00:12:19.335 --> 00:12:20.600
Of course you can,

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:23.440
if you want to you can send the money back and undo

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:25.800
the transaction but there'll be a log of the fact that

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:28.335
money was sent to you and then money was sent back.

00:12:28.335 --> 00:12:31.995
