so that we start at the beginning. All right.

00:16:31.330 --> 00:16:34.150
So the Bitcoin blockchain basically is, you know,

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:35.190
as the name implies,

00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:37.265
it's basically a sequence of blocks.

00:16:37.265 --> 00:16:41.160
Yeah. So,you can add blocks to the blockchain at will.

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:43.860
In fact, every 10 minutes, a new block is

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:47.770
created and these blocks basically form this very very long chain.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:49.065
Yeah, it's basically,

00:16:49.065 --> 00:16:50.870
from the beginning of time, you know,

00:16:50.870 --> 00:16:54.440
since 2009, these blocks have been added every 10 minutes.

00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:56.290
So there are many many many of these blocks.

00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:59.285
And the reason they form a chain is because you notice,

00:16:59.285 --> 00:17:01.945
when I looking at block number N minus one,

00:17:01.945 --> 00:17:05.620
that's the block header contains in it a bunch of transactions,

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:08.495
you can see there's a whole transaction tree that's

00:17:08.495 --> 00:17:11.230
embedded in the block in the block header.

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:14.650
This is what's called-- this tree here-- is what's called a Mercal tree,

00:17:14.650 --> 00:17:19.420
which means that essentially all of these transactions that

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:22.605
represent the block and we'll talk about transactions in just a minute,

00:17:22.605 --> 00:17:26.095
essentially they're sort of committed to in the block header.

00:17:26.095 --> 00:17:28.030
Yeah, so this

00:17:28.030 --> 00:17:33.100
value here is a hash value that commits to all the transactions that are embedded

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:34.420
in this particular block.

00:17:34.420 --> 00:17:37.650
There is what's called a non switch,

00:17:37.650 --> 00:17:39.450
is related to the proof of work,

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:40.735
I won't talk about that here.

00:17:40.735 --> 00:17:44.615
There's a time stamp but the important field in the block header is what's called a hash.

00:17:44.615 --> 00:17:48.810
So what is this hash? Basically, every block is

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:53.085
in every block what you do is you hash the block header.

00:17:53.085 --> 00:17:56.790
Yes, you compute some sort of a compressed function of the block header and then you

00:17:56.790 --> 00:18:01.020
write the resulting hash value into the hash field of the next block.

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:03.505
And this is what forms the chain structure.

00:18:03.505 --> 00:18:05.960
Yes, so you can see here again block number

00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:08.720
n contains a hash of block number n minus one,

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:11.940
block number n plus one will contain a hash of block number

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:15.730
n and so we get this very very long chain structure where

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:18.455
this hash operation

00:18:18.455 --> 00:18:23.210
induces sequence among blocks and that's why we call it a chain.

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:25.895
As I said, this is only generation one of blocked,

00:18:25.895 --> 00:18:27.325
of the block chain structure.

00:18:27.325 --> 00:18:29.285
There are many new ideas being

