it is the one that actually gets the block reward.

00:48:50.910 --> 00:48:52.610
So basically,

00:48:52.610 --> 00:48:53.890
proof of work is a

00:48:53.890 --> 00:48:57.150
one way to implement a randomness beacon

00:48:57.150 --> 00:48:59.390
that chooses a miner at random,

00:48:59.390 --> 00:49:00.660
but now

00:49:00.660 --> 00:49:02.050
there have been many proposals for

00:49:02.050 --> 00:49:05.415
other randomness beacons that actually are not that power hungry

00:49:05.415 --> 00:49:07.950
that don't require burning so much energy.

00:49:07.950 --> 00:49:09.910
So in fact, this is kind of, as I said,

00:49:09.910 --> 00:49:12.685
generation one blockchains require proof of work,

00:49:12.685 --> 00:49:14.700
the third generation blockchains are actually

00:49:14.700 --> 00:49:16.885
starting to move away from proof of work.

00:49:16.885 --> 00:49:19.785
And just to give you some examples

00:49:19.785 --> 00:49:21.770
there's a lot of,

00:49:21.770 --> 00:49:23.795
there are many experiments with proof of stake.

00:49:23.795 --> 00:49:25.800
